
## Bandit Level 17 → Level 18

**Challenge:** 

There are 2 files in the homedirectory: passwords.old and passwords.new. The password for the next level is in passwords.new and is the only line that has been changed between passwords.old and passwords.new

NOTE: if you have solved this level and see ‘Byebye!’ when trying to log into bandit18, this is related to the next level, bandit19

Commands you may need to solve this level
cat, grep, ls, diff


**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: ls
# list files in the current directory
# you should see: passwords.old and passwords.new

STEP 2: wc -l passwords.old passwords.new
# optional: confirms both files have many lines
# we need a comparison tool, not manual reading

STEP 3: diff passwords.old passwords.new
# diff compares two files line-by-line
# it prints the lines that are different

STEP 4: diff passwords.old passwords.new | grep ">"
# in diff output:
# lines starting with "<" come from the old file
# lines starting with ">" come from the new file
# the new password is the changed line in passwords.new, so we want the ">" line

STEP 5: diff passwords.old passwords.new | grep ">" | cut -c3-
# cut -c3- removes the leading "> " so you see only the password text


```
**Password:** [x2gLTTjFwMOhQ8oWNbMN362QKxfRqGlO]



**What I learned:** 

diff shows exactly what changed between two files.

diff passwords.old passwords.new → compares content line-by-line

the symbol > means lines belong to the new file

the symbol < means lines belong to the new file

cut -c3- → strips the diff marker (> ) so you get the raw password, displays from 3rd character until the end
